            <ArticleTitle>[Physical pain and suffering in the child].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>269-78; discussion 278-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Since about ten years ago there has been a great interest in the treatment of pediatric pain, previously neglected in medical practice. A review of procedures of pain assessment is made: self-assessment, behavioural analysis and biological measurements. The main therapeutic procedures are also reviewed (drugs, physical agents and psychological treatment), emphasizing the interest of prophylaxis and parental participation in children's pain treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
